theory_blocks.body:
In the Extended course, probabilities are written with letters:
- $P(A)$ is the probability of event $A$;
- $P(A')$ is the probability of *not* $A$ (“$A$ prime”, the **complement** of $A$);
- $P(A)+P(A')=1$, i.e. $P(A')=1-P(A)$.

This is exactly the complement rule from earlier in the lesson, written in function notation so it can be combined with algebra — for example, setting up an equation when several unknown probabilities must add to $1$.

