theory_blocks.body:
For events (or sets) $A$ and $B$:
- $A\cap B$ (“$A$ *and* $B$”, the **intersection**) is the overlap: both $A$ and $B$ happen;
- $A\cup B$ (“$A$ *or* $B$”, the **union**) is everything in $A$ or in $B$ or in both;
- $A'$ (“not $A$”) is everything outside $A$, so $P(A')=1-P(A)$.

$$P(A\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\cap B).$$

The subtraction corrects the double counting of the overlap — exactly the same correction as step 2 of the Venn-diagram strategy above, now written as a formula.

